==============================================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================================
  'adx21 trending' held at +0.239 R — and it is REJECTED.

  ADX at three smoothings, held out, against the same base:
    ADX(7)  trending   +0.022
    ADX(14) trending   -0.071      (round one, same cut)
    ADX(21) trending   +0.239

  ONE LENGTH OUT OF THREE WORKS and the other two are flat or
  negative. That is a parameter search landing on a lucky value,
  and this file said so before the run: 'if ADX only works at
  one length out of three, that is fitting, not a finding.'

  Compare round one, where the finding was REAL: EMA and
  supertrend are DIFFERENT indicators measuring the same idea,
  and both held at the same size with symmetric losing
  counter-sides. Here it is the SAME indicator at three
  settings, and only one of them agrees with itself.

  Passing a held-out test is necessary, not sufficient. A
  pre-registered falsification rule exists so that a number
  which clears the bar can still be turned down.

  EVERYTHING ELSE IN ROUND TWO IS NOISE: turnover +0.005/-0.010,
  volatility +0.044, BB width +0.067, BB position +0.037.

  AND THE BOLLINGER PREDICTION FAILED, which is worth recording
  because it was made in writing before the run. The stated
  mechanism was that an entry taken OUTSIDE the band should do
  better, since a snap-back has somewhere to go. Outside the band
  came back at -0.199 held out — the wrong sign, not merely small.
  The one family here with a mechanism argued in advance is the one
  that most clearly failed.

  SO NOTHING SURVIVES ON TOP OF THE TREND FILTER. The model is ONE
  filter deep and the second layer is empty — which is what
  twenty-one previously failed entry filters in this project would
  have predicted, and what round one's own warning said to expect.
